          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "jiǎndāo is built from two parts inherited from Middle Chinese (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription): tsjenX, glossed 'to cut off' and 'to make even', and taw, the word for a knife: a cutting knife."
            }
          ]
        },
